WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
Let's get into first principles daily, episode 28 for July 3, 2026.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.460
Closing the week with one more look at where the next 10 times is hiding.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.220
A century after insulin's patent sold for a dollar,

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.560
vials still list for hundreds despite raw material costs in the low single digits.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:25.440
A single vial of analog insulin that reaches a pharmacy counter at several hundred dollars

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.760
contains a few dollars worth of amino acids, salts and growth media when the atoms are

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.400
counted at commodity prices.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.040
The gap is not explained by the chemistry of recombinant protein production, which has

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.660
been scaled for decades in other biologics.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:47.000
Instead, the price reflects layers of regulatory exclusivity, device patents, and distribution

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.940
contracts that sit on top of the molecule itself.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.140
That separation between the physical floor and the observed price is the opening for first

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.480
principles examination.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.900
The surprise grows once the manufacturing sequence is laid out.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:08.340
Engineered cells ferment the protein, chromatography isolates it, and sterile filling packages it.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.200
All steps already performed at industrial volumes for comparable molecules.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.440
The difference lies in what happens after the vial is sealed.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.720
Insulin manufacturing begins with engineered E. coli or yeast strains that express the protein

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.540
in large bio-reactors.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.160
This is followed by purification, formulation, and filling into vials or cartridges.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.760
The process itself is mature.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:39.360
Comparable therapeutic proteins are produced at industrial scale for other indications at

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.280
far lower unit costs once volume and competition are present.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.480
What keeps insulin prices elevated is a set of institutional overlays that have accumulated

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.580
since the 1980s.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:56.780
Ever-greening through incremental formulation changes and new delivery devices has allowed

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:02.260
successive layers of patent protection even after the original recombinant patents expired.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:09.200
Peninjectors in particular carry device patents that extend exclusivity years beyond the drug

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:09.720
substance.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:16.200
Pharmacy benefit managers negotiate rebates that are opaque to patients and that favor list

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.900
price inflation followed by confidential discounts.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:25.460
State and federal regulations on vial similar approval pathways add further delay.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:30.880
Although an abbreviated route exists, demonstrating similarity for a biologic

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.880
still requires substantial clinical data packages.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.700
The result is a market in which three originator companies have maintained

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.480
dominant share for decades with limited entry by competitors.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.760
List prices in the United States therefore reflect these accumulated frictions rather than

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:54.780
marginal production expense. Hospitals and insurers see net costs after rebates

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:00.340
that are lower than the sticker price yet uninsured or high deductible patients encounter the

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.680
full amount. The system stabilized around this equilibrium because each participant

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.280
optimized within the existing rules rather than questioning the rules themselves.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.200
One objection often raised is that safety demands these controls.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:22.680
Yet other recombinant proteins reached lower unit costs under the same FDA framework once patent

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:28.740
and reimbursement barriers were lower. Another layer is the specialized filling equipment required

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:35.360
for cartridges and pens. Lines must be validated for each device format and those validation costs

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.940
are recovered across fewer units when competition is limited.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.920
Carrying costs compound because inventory sits in a distribution chain whose contracts reward

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:51.720
high list prices. Each of these steps adds real expense inside the current frame, but none is

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:58.240
required by the fermentation or purification chemistry itself. A rough magic wand estimate

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:05.080
begins with the primary inputs. The insulin molecule itself is a 51 amino acid peptide

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:11.760
whose constituent amino acids at bulk commodity prices amount to well under a dollar program.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.060
A typical vial contains roughly 1000 units or about 36 milligrams of protein,

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:25.940
so the amino acid value sits on the order of a few cents. Growth media, salts, water for injection

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:31.020
and ecccipients add perhaps another dollar or two when purchased at industrial scale.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:37.960
Downstream processing, chromatography resins, filtration membranes, and energy for bioreactors

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:44.460
and liofylicers adds further cost, but these are amortized across thousands of liters of annual

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:50.600
production in existing facilities. Published analyses of contract manufacturing for similar

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:57.100
monoclonal antibodies and therapeutic proteins place fully formulated bulk biologic drug substance

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:03.820
in the low tens of dollars per gram at commercial scale. Applying that benchmark to insulin yields

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:09.840
a finished vial cost estimate in the low single digit dollars once filling, stoppering, and quality

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:16.120
release are included. That places the magic wand floor somewhere between roughly three and eight

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:22.360
dollars per vial under current technology, with the exact figure sensitive to volume and facility

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:29.500
utilization. Against the U.S. list price that has ranged from 100 to 300 dollars or more in recent

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:37.180
years, the implied idiot index therefore lies between roughly 15 and 100. To arrive at that range,

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:43.940
divide the observed list price by the estimated floor. 100 dollars divided by eight dollars gives

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:51.400
roughly 12, while 300 dollars divided by three dollars reaches 100. The gap does not reside primarily

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:57.400
in the bio reactor or purification suite. Those steps have already been driven down by decades of

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:04.420
biologics manufacturing experience. Instead, the largest increments appear in regulatory and legal overhead.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.900
In the specialized filling lines qualified for pens and cartridges, and in the distribution

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:16.400
and rebate machinery that sits between manufacturer and patient. Each of these layers adds cost

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:22.300
that is real within the current institutional frame yet is not dictated by the physics of protein

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:29.600
synthesis or the thermodynamics of fermentation. An objection sometimes offered is that quality control

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:36.280
testing itself is expensive. Yet the same testing burden applies to other biologics whose prices have

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:42.620
fallen farther once market entry increased. The arithmetic therefore points away from the reactor

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:49.020
and toward the rules that govern how many reactors can operate at full utilization. A redesign

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:53.860
effort would therefore begin by separating the molecule from its surrounding apparatus.

00:06:54.540 --> 00:07:01.660
The first concrete target is regulatory. Establishing a clearer, lower cost pathway for interchangeable

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:07.740
biosimilars that treats insulin more like a standardized therapeutic protein than a novel biologic.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:14.540
The second target is device independence. De-coupling the drug substance from proprietary pen

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:20.440
mechanisms so that lower cost, vial, and syringe, or standardized cartridge formats can compete

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:27.260
on equal footing. The third target is transparency in the supply chain, requiring that net prices

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:33.140
after rebates be visible at the point of sale, which would reduce the incentive for list price

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:39.460
inflation. Each of these moves requires policy or contractual change rather than new chemistry.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:45.460
The genuinely hard constraint is demonstrating long-term safety and immunosignacity

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:51.320
equivalence at the volumes needed for diabetes care. That step cannot be wished away.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.780
Yet once equivalence is accepted, the remaining cost reduction follows from volume,

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:02.080
competition, and the removal of artificial scarcity created by patent thickets.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:07.480
The prize is a price trajectory that tracks the established learning curve of other

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:12.480
recombinant proteins rather than remaining anchored to legacy distribution arrangements.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:18.160
A further practical requirement is that any new entrant must secure a reliable

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.760
bioreactor capacity without triggering fresh device patent litigation.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:29.320
That sequencing matters because capacity alone does not lower price if exclusivity on the

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:35.680
delivery format persists. Policy changes that shortened clinical data requirements for interchange

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:41.540
ability would also need to preserve post-market surveillance so that any rare immunosignacity

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:48.200
signal can still be detected at scale. When the dominant cost of a molecule lies outside its

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.960
atoms and its reactors, the redesigned target shifts from the production line to the

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:58.760
rules that govern entry and reimbursement. The second principle is that an idiot index

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:04.000
measured in tens or hundreds signals an institutional rather than a materials problem.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:09.520
Only changes to those institutions move the price measurably closer to the floor.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:14.580
Consider what that means in practice. If the physical inputs and the established

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:20.900
manufacturing steps already sit at a handful of dollars, then every additional layer of exclusivity,

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:27.200
opacity or specialized validation is an accumulated friction that can be examined one by one.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:33.320
The same pattern shows up whenever a biologic or any other engineered product carries an idiot

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:39.700
index well above ten. The question becomes whether the next reduction comes from a new reactor

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:45.700
design or from a rule change that lets existing reactors run at higher utilization under genuine

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:51.660
competition. That distinction matters because the first approach improves the atoms while the

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:57.360
second approach improves the market that surrounds the atoms. In the insulin case, the arithmetic

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:03.720
already points to the market side. Tomorrow, the show examines another domain where the same separation

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:09.060
between physical cost and observed price creates an opening for first principles work.

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:15.240
Who will be the first to publish a transparent high-volume biosimilar insulin cost model

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:20.880
that regulators and payers can actually use? That's first principles daily for today.

